cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or CHORD, please cite the AT-AF3 manuscript."
title: "AT-AF3: Associative Thinking Enables Zero-Shot D-Protein Structure Generation"
abstract: >-
  AT-AF3 is a zero-shot framework for controlling stereochemistry in frozen
  AlphaFold 3 predictions. Associative Thinking compiles chirality requirements
  and residue-level chemical knowledge into CCD constraints, followed by
  deterministic geometric verification and correction. The CHORD benchmark
  contains seven All-D and nine Local-D targets evaluated with 30 matched
  inference seeds per target.
